 over a denominator pool of 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8), F06 (1 to 4 over the same pool), F10 (1 to 7) and F15, F16, F13 (1 to 7) are not constrained to be less than the denominator, so question stems, options and keyed answers can show fractions above one whole. F13 also prints the denominator over the numerator, a reversed notation. F17 can print a numerator of 6 or 7 over a denominator of 2. F07 prints numerator values 1 to 4 and denominator values 3 to 5 and 8 in the same hint, so a numerator above its denominator is observed to be printable. F12 joins a denominator with a cardinal word plus 'ths' (for example one, two, three and five produce non-words), and F19's fixed list prints such non-words and improper fractions as options. F14 has independent get and ordinal domains, and its ordinal list mixes singular and plural forms with no coupling, so keyed answers and choices can read as ungrammatical forms such as 'halfs' combined with a number word or a singular ordinal after 'two'. F11 prints F14 text, so it inherits this. F18, F01, F02, F03, F04, F08, F09 print only curriculum-gated vocabulary or observed values that are proper and grammatical; the observed F18 answer values include no improper fraction.\"}",
